# Local app and cost data tables

The site is the Next.js app in `nextjs-app/`. Content comes from Sanity project `hoc4qxji`.

## Which server to open

- Current content work uses `npm run dev:staging` from `nextjs-app/`. That loads `.env.staging` (dataset `staging-2026`) and does not load `.env.local`.
- `npm run dev` uses `.env.local` (dataset `production`).
- Read the running terminal for the printed Local URL. Next starts on port 3000 and uses the next free port if 3000 is taken.
- The homepage is Sanity slug `home`, served at `/`. The `costsMaps` block is on that page.

## Map Description table

- Accordion title `Map Description/Data Table` and its column labels are in `nextjs-app/app/components/blocks/CostsMaps.tsx` (`tableColumns`).
- `CostsMaps` renders a loading placeholder until it mounts, so the table is absent from the first HTML response. Confirm a header in the hydrated DOM (text `Map Description/Data Table`), not with curl.

## Similar tables

Change only the table the request names:

- `JitterPlot.tsx` — `Chart Description/Data Table`, column `Per Capita Cost`
- `CostsBreakdown.tsx` and `PayerBreakdown.tsx` — `Chart Description/Data Table`, their own column labels
